# V2 ONLINE DRESS STORE ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# 1. Production Supabase PostgreSQL & Auth Credentials
# =============================================================================
# Configure these to connect to your production Supabase database.
# When provided, all admin authentication is validated server-side by Supabase
# Auth and enforced by PostgreSQL Row Level Security (RLS) policies.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# CRITICAL SECURITY NOTE:
# Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or plaintext database passwords here!
# The anon key only allows access permitted by Row Level Security (RLS).

# =============================================================================
# 2. Local / Staging Sandbox Admin Credentials (Optional)
# =============================================================================
# When Supabase is not configured, the platform runs in local sandbox mode.
# Plaintext passwords must NEVER be placed here.
# Instead, store the SHA-256 salted hash:
# hash = sha256("<password>:<salt>") where salt is "v2_boutique_salt_2026"
#
# Default initial test credential hashes (admin1234 / admin1234):
# VITE_ADMIN_USERNAME_HASH=96115dc05b04dfa3c7ea6b4419f160839f0b9ad08bde87016a7b00966f674580
# VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=96115dc05b04dfa3c7ea6b4419f160839f0b9ad08bde87016a7b00966f674580
